asive responses in political discourse. The task is grounded in an expert-designed two-level taxonomy and a benchmark dataset of question-answer pairs from U.S. presidential interviews, requiring systems to distinguish clear from evasive responses at a coarse level and identify one of nine fine-grained evasion strategies at a fine-grained level.\n"
